change('main',r'After $t_i$ queries on row $i$, let $\ell_i$ be their observed flip sum. The remaining scores imply',r'Each output is a row of the score matrix. After $t_i$ queries on row $i$, let $\ell_i$ be their observed flip sum. Bounding each unobserved count between zero and $p_i$ gives',[38])
old=main.split('The completion model places')[1].split('\n\n')[0]
change('main','The completion model places'+old,r'Our completion model imposes no cross-entry constraints on unknown scores. This is an adversarial completion assumption, not statistical independence of evaluators. Assigning all unknown entries their zero-flip endpoints realizes the full lower-cost vector; maximum-flip endpoints realize the upper-cost vector. The retention bounds are therefore sharp for both pooling rules. Section~\ref{sec:median} additionally characterizes minimum median certificate size.',[39])
change('main',r'Zero-cost nonselected decisions may be included for free. Sorting the selected costs computes $V(w)$. Set $V^-=V(u)$ and $V^+=V(\ell)$.',r'Sorting selected-output costs computes $V(w)$. Set the safe count $V^-=V(u)$ and optimistic count $V^+=V(\ell)$.',[40])
